# Advanced ORM

## Framework semantics

Complex filtering often needs subqueries/`exists`, association filtering via `matching`, QueryExpression callbacks, and denormalized counters via CounterCache. Prefer Query expressions and bindings over string SQL. `Connection::execute` is a last resort for application domain work.

## Required behavior

- Encapsulate advanced query shapes in finders on the owning Table.
- Prefer `matching` / `notMatching` / subquery expressions over ad-hoc joins in controllers.
- Build complex `WHERE` with `where(function (QueryExpression $exp, SelectQuery $q) { … })` and bindings — not concatenated request data.
- Use CounterCache (or equivalent Behavior) for maintained counts — not controller increments.
- Keep raw SQL / `Connection::execute` exceptional, isolated, and fully bound; never concatenate user input.
- When using `updateAll` / `deleteAll` / query `update`/`delete`, document that entity callbacks and application rules may not run.

## Anti-patterns

- Controller-built subquery graphs copied everywhere
- Manual counter updates scattered across actions when CounterCache fits
- Unbound string SQL / bypassing ORM for convenience
- Treating bulk SQL APIs as drop-in `save()` replacements when lifecycle matters

## Review checklist

- [ ] Advanced queries live in finders
- [ ] Counters have a single ownership strategy
- [ ] No SQL injection vectors
- [ ] Bulk vs entity-save tradeoffs are explicit
